requires 1.4.5
# The line above stops Siril unless it is version 1.4.5 or newer; without it Siril skips every line.
# AstroPlanner Processing Coach, script 2 of 2 (stack): apply your frame choice and stack.
# Run it after script 1, with the same night folder as Siril's working folder and this file's
# full path after -s, e.g.
#   siril-cli -d "<night folder>" -s "<folder you saved it in>/astroplanner-stack.ssf"
# A bare file name after -s is looked up in the night folder, not in the terminal's current folder.
# In Siril itself: set the working folder to the night folder, add the folder holding this file
# to the script folders in Preferences (Scripts), then choose the script from the Scripts menu.
# Your choice: Siril's 80 % roundness filter. The coach expects it to keep 812 frames (2 h 15 min).
# It writes only into process-coach/: about 20.2 GB more for the 812 aligned frames, plus the stack.
# Move into process-coach/, where script 1 left the aligned sequence.
cd process-coach
# Write an aligned copy (r_pp_light_) of each frame that passes your choice; frames Siril could
# not align are always left out. Siril counts this percentage over all the frames, including any
# it could not align, so it can keep more than 80 % of the aligned ones.
seqapplyreg pp_light -filter-round=80%
# Average the kept frames into result_coach.fit. With 812 frames (the coach's rule of thumb
# for sigma clipping is 30 or more), winsorized clipping at 3 and 3 drops values that
# show up in only a few frames, such as satellite trails and hot pixels.
# Additive normalisation with scaling evens out changes in sky level; the result is scaled to
# 0 to 1 and the three colour channels are balanced.
stack r_pp_light rej w 3 3 -norm=addscale -output_norm -rgb_equal -out=result_coach
# Release the sequence. result_coach.fit in process-coach/ is your stack for the next steps.
close
